title op6: a split against a delta of one

# Shape two of four for the PENDING set-delta proposal.  See
# op6-split-quiet.tree for the gold policy: gold is today's answer,
# and the comment states what the proposal would change.
#
# Onto un-shares z.  Off-of renames one name, x to aa, so the delta
# is lost {x} gained {aa}.
#
# Today Definition 9.3 pairs the single gained name with the single
# lost one -- the only case it can read -- and routes the rename to
# the fragment holding x, which is pool 10.  Clean.
#
# Under the proposal the answer is the same and the reasoning is
# shorter: with one lost and one gained the pairing is forced by the
# sets themselves, so no recognition step is involved at all.  The
# proposal keeps routing exactly where routing is determined.
#
# Today: clean, pool 10 holds aa and y, the split fragment holds z.
# Under the proposal: identical.
#
# The corpus already contains this shape as the one-rename/ arm of
# 6-ambiguous-succession.tree.  It is repeated here on its own so
# that the four op6 shapes can be read as a set, and so that a change
# to it cannot hide inside a fixture that also covers something else.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      10-100: z

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: aa = v0
      10-100: y
      10-100: z

# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect clean

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared
      10-100: aa = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0
